2. Multithreading (Thread Level)
Sample Answer:
"Multithreading is when a single program performs multiple tasks at the same time using threads.
  Each thread is like a lightweight process within the program and shares the same memory.
  For example, in a browser, one thread loads images while another handles user clicks.
  This improves the program’s efficiency and responsiveness."

